name: {{SKILL_NAME}}
description: >-
  Build or extend {{PROJECT_NAME}} through the {{PRESET}} game pipeline when the user invokes {{INVOCATION}}, /{{PREFIX}}, or asks to make this game or run its development workflow.
---

Read `{{AGENT_DIR}}/commands/{{PREFIX}}.md` from the game repository root, then load
only the selected runbook and its declared contracts. Arguments following
`{{INVOCATION}}` are the orchestrator's selectors and modifiers.

Read `{{ROOT_DOC}}` and `{{MEMORY_PATH}}/MEMORY.md` when present. Memory is
append-only. Resolve all runtime and role paths from the game repository root,
even when the shell starts in a subdirectory. Never bootstrap inside the generator.

When a runbook says to spawn a specialist, use its native `.codex/agents/*.toml`
adapter if the harness supports named agents. Otherwise read the matching
`.codex/agents/*.md` and pass its body and bounded task to `spawn_agent` (or the
available collaboration tool). Inherit model settings. Wait for its structured
result before dependent work. Parallelize only independent tasks with distinct
write ownership. Reviewers and verifiers remain read-only and independent of
the implementation. If delegation is unavailable, report that limitation before
an implementation workflow requiring independent review; do not claim a self-review
is independent. Read-only routing and gates can run without delegation.

<!-- engine:2d -->
For art, use the available native image generation tool after STYLE LOCK, then
register its returned file using the art adapter. If native generation is absent,
present the rendered prompt and wait for an externally produced image. A rendered
prompt is not a generated image, and human STYLE LOCK approval is always required.
<!-- /engine:2d -->
<!-- engine:3d -->
For 3D art, use the Blender recipe/spec workflow in contract-3d.md. Image tools
may supply concept references and textures; record provenance with image-register.
Inspect Blender previews and real Godot screenshots. STYLE LOCK requires human
approval before production. A whole-game request selects --build and continues
through staged board items until the approved brief is delivered.
<!-- /engine:3d -->

Shell scripts must be invoked with Bash, including on Windows. Check each gate's
JSON `pass` value; exit code zero alone does not mean the gate passed.
